{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorAmphicheiral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorAmphicheiral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_amphicheiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_amphicheiral","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L46-L94","doc":"**Corollary (amphicheiral knot factor).**\n\nUnder the amphicheiral hypothesis, every non-alternating block\ncontributes its own square `w_μ · (χ_μ(β)/χ_μ(𝟙))²` — the mirror\nis invisible there — while the alternating block contributes\n`-w_alt · h²`, `h = altRatio β alt`.  With the Plancherel\nnormalisation `off_block_norm` on the non-alternating blocks,\n\n  `a_K(β, β*) = 1 - w_alt · (1 + h²)` .\n\n**This is not the manuscript's displayed `a = 1 - h²`, and the\ndifference is not a rearrangement.**  The displayed form needs the\nnon-alternating blocks to sum to `1`; `off_block_norm` as stated\n(and as the `.ts` block's `computation` probe checks it) sums them\nto `1 - w_alt`, which leaves the extra `-w_alt` above.  They\ncoincide only at `w_alt = 0`, where both sides are `1` and the\ncorollary says nothing about `h`.  Recorded rather than reconciled:\nwhich of the two normalisations the chapter intends is an authoring\nquestion, not one this file can settle.  See `cor:knot-factor-amphicheiral`.\n\nThe statement replaces `∃ a, a = …`, which held for every `β`,\n`β_mirror` and `altPartition` and so used neither hypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:knot-factor-amphicheiral","label":"cor:knot-factor-amphicheiral","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-amphicheiral.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.altRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.altRatio","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The alternating-block character ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.alt_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.alt_block","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.off_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.off_block","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.alt_in","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.alt_in","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral.mk","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Amphicheiral","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorAmphicheiral.lean#L29-L39","doc":"**Amphicheirality hypothesis.**\n\n`β · β*` reproduces `β · β` on every block except the alternating\nblock `(1^n)`, where the mirror flips sign. ","signatureChunk":0}]}